---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Greetings, Traveler!</h1>
			<p>
				Welcome to my graphics programming projects diary! 
			</p>
			<p>
				The purpose of this site is to document my progress as I explore graphics programming
				through developing a series of projects:-
			</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Software Rasterized Renderer</li>
				<li>Software Path Tracer</li>
				<li>Hardware Accelerated Renderer</li>
				<li>Advanced Real-Time Graphics Engine</li>
			</ol>
			<p>
				The above list is purely a means to give me a direction, and is liable to change and extend as I progress. 
				I plan to add subheadings to the list as I go along, so that it can serve as a useful index as well.
			</p>
			<p>
				Documenting my progress and presenting it in a clear manner has other benefits besides preserving a record
				of my work and thoughts. It's slow, reflective and creative nature allows me to internalize the concepts that I'm
				learning and helps me address any gaps in my understanding. Additionally, it serves as a useful tool for revision.
			</p>
			<p>
				I'm trying to avoid tutorials and instead focusing on building up knowledge from basic principles. Here are some of
				the resources/books that I'm using:-
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="https://a.co/d/0hPuhA8i">Fundamentals of Computer Graphics: International Student Edition</a></li> 
				(Steve Marschner, Peter Shirley)
				<li><a href="https://a.co/d/0ifMgzxu">Real-Time Rendering, Fourth Edition</a></li> 
				(Tomas Akenine-M&ouml;ller, Eric Haines, Naty Hoffman)
				<li><a href="https://www.realtimerendering.com/">Real-Time Rendering website</a></li>
				<li><a href="https://immersivemath.com/ila/index.html">Immersive Linear Algebra</a></li>
				(J. Str&ouml;m, K. &Aring;str&ouml;m, and T. Akenine-M&ouml;ller)
			</ul>
			<p>
				I intend to post as often as possible; hopefully I can do it several times per week, if life permits.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
